{"name":"Lime Coco Cake","hex":"#e6efcc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lime","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any inorganic material containing calcium, usually calcium oxide (quicklime) or calcium hydroxide (slaked lime).","Any gluey or adhesive substance that traps or captures; sometimes a synonym for birdlime."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To treat with calcium hydroxide or calcium oxide (lime).","To smear with birdlime.\n To ensnare, catch, entrap."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lime"},{"term":"coco","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Coconut palm.","Coconut, the fruit of the coconut palm."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coco"},{"term":"cake","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rich, sweet dessert food, typically made of flour, sugar, and eggs and baked in an oven, and often covered in icing.","A small mass of baked dough, especially a thin loaf from unleavened dough."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Coat (something) with a crust of solid material.","To form into a cake, or mass."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cake"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cake","blocks":[{"text":"Cake is a baker's confectionery made by combining flour with a liquid, a fat or both, and usually with a leavening agent. Cakes are usually baked, but can be griddled. In their oldest forms, cakes were modifications of bread, but cakes now cover a wide range of preparations that can be simple or elaborate and which share features with other desserts such as pastries, meringues, custards, and pies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Pound_layer_cake.jpg/330px-Pound_layer_cake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cake","wikidata":"Q13276"},{"title":"Lime (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lime is a color that is a shade of yellow-green, so named because it is a representation of the color of the citrus fruit lime. It is the color that is in between the web color chartreuse and yellow on the color wheel. Alternate names for this color included yellow-green, lemon-lime, lime green, or bitter lime."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/AosaHGkyuai_%28cropped%29_3.jpg/330px-AosaHGkyuai_%28cropped%29_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lime_(color)","wikidata":"Q906936"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Bartolom%C3%A9_Esteban_Perez_Murillo_-_Baking_of_Flat_Cakes_-_WGA16350.jpg/500px-Bartolom%C3%A9_Esteban_Perez_Murillo_-_Baking_of_Flat_Cakes_-_WGA16350.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Bartolom%C3%A9_Esteban_Perez_Murillo_-_Baking_of_Flat_Cakes_-_WGA16350.jpg/500px-Bartolom%C3%A9_Esteban_Perez_Murillo_-_Baking_of_Flat_Cakes_-_WGA16350.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Baking of Flat Cakes by the Spanish painter Bartolomé Esteban Murillo, c. 1650","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABartolom%C3%A9_Esteban_Perez_Murillo_-_Baking_of_Flat_Cakes_-_WGA16350.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Cake_mix_in_plastic_packet_photo.JPG/500px-Cake_mix_in_plastic_packet_photo.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Cake_mix_in_plastic_packet_photo.JPG/500px-Cake_mix_in_plastic_packet_photo.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chocolate cake mix in plastic packets","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACake_mix_in_plastic_packet_photo.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/182365_Gooey_Butter_Cake.jpg/500px-182365_Gooey_Butter_Ca